{
  "name": "auto-reply-ig relay",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## auto-reply-ig relay\n\n**Setup (3 steps)**\n1. Create a **Header Auth** credential named `auto-reply-ig API key`: Name = `Authorization`, Value = `Bearer <API key from the app: Settings > n8n>`. Select it on the two HTTP Request nodes.\n2. In the **Config** node, set `appUrl` to your app's public URL (no trailing slash). Skipped if you downloaded the workflow from the app.\n3. Activate the workflow and paste the **Production URL** of the webhook nodes into Meta > Webhooks > Callback URL.\n\nThe app does all keyword matching and sending. This workflow only relays Meta's requests, so it works for every post and keyword.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "5f3f0a51-0001-4a00-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky: Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-240, -120]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Do not re-serialize the body.**\nMeta signs the exact bytes it sends. The POST webhook has **Raw Body** on, and the Code node forwards the original string untouched. Changing it (e.g. JSON.stringify) breaks the HMAC check in the app.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "5f3f0a51-0002-4a00-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Sticky: Raw body",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [220, -120]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Extend here.** Add your own nodes after the event relay (e.g. Google Sheets log, Slack/Telegram alert, CRM). Each item is one comment result: `commentId`, `status`, `matchedKeyword`, `error`.",
        "height": 160,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "5f3f0a51-0003-4a00-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Sticky: Extend",
